Basically only three facts need to be established by the claimants for assessing compensation in the case of death :
(a) age of the deceased;
(b) income of the deceased; and the (c) the number of dependents.

Having regard to the facts and circumstances of the case, it is hereby ordered that total compensation amount is disbursed as follows :
(a) Petitioner No.1/Smt. Sarita (Wife of deceased Kanhya Singh @ Kanhey Singh)
shall be entitled to share amount of Rs.10,00,000 (Rupees Ten Lakhs Only)
alongwith proportionate interest;
(b) Petitioner No.2/daughter Khushboo (minor daughter of deceased Kanhya Singh @ Kanhey Singh) shall be entitled to share amount of Rs.6,00,000 including the share amount of petitioner no.4 Upendra Singh @ Rs.2,00,000 and the share amount of petitioner No.4/Jamuni Devi @ Rs.5,00,000, thus having a total amount Smt. Sarita vs Sh. Achchhey Lal Yadav on 6 May, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/162897943/
12 of Rs. 13,00,000/ (Rupees Thirteen Lakhs Only) alongwith proportionate interest;

(c) Petitioner No.3/son Mayank Raj (minor son of deceased Kanhya Singh @ Kanhey Singh) shall be entitled to share amount of Rs.6,00,000 (Rupees Six Lakhs Only)
alongwith proportionate interest;
(a) Petitioner/injured Smt. Sarita, (in caseIII) shall be entitled to share amount of Rs.15,000 (Rupees Fifteen Thousand Only) alongwith proportionate interest;
MACT No. 743/19, 278/20 & 279/20 Sarita Devi & Ors. v. Achchey Lal Yadav & Ors.
49.

